{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493930-metis-and-aggravated-damage","id":1493930,"title":"Metis and Aggravated Damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-28T14:22:25-07:00","id":1493930,"title":"Metis and Aggravated Damage","content":"In the W20 combat chapter under aggravated damage, it says Garou may soak aggravated damage except in their breed form. There is no exception made for Metis to soak it in Crinos. I believe this is a copy and paste mistake from revised which I have been told had a similar wording but an FAQ in the storyteller manual stating that Metis could soak. Is there any way to get this errata'd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T14:29:38-07:00","id":1493932,"title":"","content":"The odds of that getting addressed officially are basically 0 at this point unfortunately. Go with the Rev ST FAQ, your players making Crinos-born already have enough stacked against them in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T16:09:52-07:00","id":1494000,"title":"","content":"Metis would very much be a footnote in Garou history if they never could soak aggravated. I've got no idea why anyone would ever play one considering that they'd be deader than dirt and unlikely to even get past the Rite of Passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T16:24:14-07:00","id":1494001,"title":"","content":"Technically, the way Rev. and W20 Core wrote it, Metis soak agg, just not in Crinos, which means they should just be fighting in Hispo.<br /> <br /> The whole thing is vastly over complicated, but the OP doesn't need to hear me spout off on it again without at least asking me to do so first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}